To remove the target character from the input string s and print the new string.
Using stringbuilder
Using recursion

Input
Maria
a
Output
mri

Code:
import java.util.*;
public class Main {
    public static void main(String[] args) {
      Scanner sc=new Scanner(System.in);
      String s=sc.nextLine();
      char target=sc.next().charAt(0);
      s=s.toLowerCase();
      int i=0;
      StringBuilder sb=new StringBuilder();
      int n=s.length();
      System.out.print(check(s,target,i,sb,n));
    }
    private static String check(String s,char target, int i,StringBuilder sb,int n){
      if(i==n){
        return sb.toString();
      }
      if(s.charAt(i)!=target){
        sb.append(s.charAt(i));
      }
      return check(s,target,i+1,sb,n);

    }
}
